## Git
docs: harness-agnostic AIOS plan, rounds 1-2 of Codex review folded in

Round 1 (REVISE, 6 high) inverted the architecture: ~/.claude/skills is its
own git repo and must be canonical; the pool and codex dirs are generated views.
Round 2 (REVISE, 2 high) caught that views published only 7 of 61 skills and
that a single rollback tarball would corrupt the canonical repo.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>, docs: fold round 3 Codex review into the AIOS plan

Round 3 (REVISE, 2 high) caught two defects introduced by round 2's own
fixes: a task-ordering deadlock between the sync guard and the symlink
inversion, and a path-traversal rm -rf fed from the writable view manifest.
Also fixes the negative-only frontmatter check (overlap, not containment),
gives the PowerShell twin full manifest semantics, and rewrites rollback
by migration phase.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>, docs: fold round 4 Codex review into the AIOS plan

R4-01 wildcard metacharacters in a manifest line reached PowerShell's
wildcard-aware -Path; all manifest-derived ops now use -LiteralPath and
glob chars are refused. R4-02 archive failures were suppressed before a
delete and both views shared one archive path; archival must now succeed
into a per-view directory or the run aborts. R4-03 rollback no longer
runs a sync that rejects the layout it just restored. R4-04 copy
freshness now hashes contents instead of comparing sizes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>, docs: fold round 5 Codex review into the AIOS plan

R5-01: deleting a canonical skill left its generated view symlink dangling
(-e is false for a broken link), while the name was dropped from the
ownership manifest - permanent untracked debris reporting zero drift.
Retirement now tests -e OR -L, archives with cp -RP so a dangling link
archives without its target, retains ownership of refused entries, and the
audit gains pool_dangling/codex_dangling. Archive dirs are no longer hidden.
Verified end to end against the plan's own script.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>, docs: Codex APPROVED the AIOS plan after 6 rounds

Findings by round: 10 -> 9 -> 7 -> 4 -> 1 -> 0.
High severity: 6 -> 2 -> 2 -> 2 -> 0 -> 0.
Gate A satisfied; Task 1 may begin. Gates B, C, D still apply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
git, push, Task 1 complete: snapshot + AMEND-01 (two-hop vendored chain)

Verifying the snapshot found four canonical entries are a two-hop symlink
chain into ~/.agents/vendor-review/claudex-loop/, which was outside the
VIEWS tarball - the canonical count restored as 57, not 61. Tarball now
includes vendor-review.

Those four are also ALREADY committed to erash11/claude-skills as
mode-120000 symlinks and pushed, i.e. the R3 breakage the plan exists to
prevent, already live and dead on Windows. Plan amended in 6 places to
untrack + gitignore them rather than vendor them into the repo, matching
the existing rule for plugin skills.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
git, fix: R7-01..R7-05, one declared vendor inventory everywhere

Codex round 7 found AMEND-01 was incomplete:
- R7-01 blanket symlink-skip also waved the 15 ordinary outward links past
  the R1 guard; now an explicit VENDORED allowlist with target verification.
- R7-02 gitignore patterns ended in '/', which matches directories, not
  symlinks - git add -A (here and in daily-backup.ps1) would have re-added
  all four. Anchored patterns + a check-ignore verification step.
- R7-03 PowerShell twin gets the same vendor policy.
- R7-04 cron wrapper still read the renamed metric key; every monthly run
  would have aborted before writing a row. Added a key-agreement check.
- R7-05 counts reconciled: 57 owned / 4 vendored / 58 published. codex-review
  removed from the frontmatter edit list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>, diff, Task 2 complete: prune the stale pool mirror (306 -> 208)

98 skills archived yesterday from ~/.claude/skills were still live in
~/.agents/skills, the folder Pi auto-discovers. Both guards clean; the
~150 third-party installs and _shared untouched. Reversible.

Also fixes three inversion-count expectations Codex surfaced before its
usage limit: the guard now FATALs on 15 links not 19, the inverter
reports inverted:15 skipped:4, and 4 vendored links legitimately remain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
git, commit, add, fetch, pull, baseline: one file, one tracked link (pre-hook), fix: R9-01..R9-07, reconcile before sync, per-machine exclude, pre-commit hook

Claude review round 9:
- R9-01 a real sync ran before reconciling memory-write/meeting-sync, whose
  pool copies hold edits found nowhere else. Task 4 now reconciles first.
- R9-02 the generated ignore list lived in the tracked, shared .gitignore;
  each machine would erase the other's list. Now .git/info/exclude.
- R9-03 pre-commit hook refuses adding/changing symlinks, allows removal.
- R9-04 inventory marks the inversion-era rollback superseded; adds
  rollback by task.
- R9-05 xargs -a (GNU-only) -> git rm --pathspec-from-file.
- R9-06 dangling third-party links now enumerated and excluded.
- R9-07 piuser gets its own primary group; not-world-readable was the
  wrong test.

Verified by running on /bin/bash 3.2: exclude block, RESUME.md kept,
.gitignore unchanged, dangling link excluded, idempotent rerun, guard,
no-repo path; hook T1-T4; pwsh parse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
git, baseline
