HOME=/tmp/sg5, fix: R10-01..R10-03, backup reports refused commits, sync unstages links

Claude review round 10:
- R10-01 the pre-commit hook's refusal was invisible: daily-backup.ps1
  discarded git commit's exit code and logged 'committed', and a link
  already staged by git add -A stayed staged. New Task 3 Step 5c patches
  Sync-Repo to check the commit (nothing-stageable is not an error), and
  both sync scripts remove third-party links from the index with
  git rm --cached, never a reset to HEAD.
- R10-02 remaining .gitignore wording now says .git/info/exclude.
- R10-03 dseditgroup check added for piuser; staff has no nested groups
  on this Mac (premise checked, did not hold).
- Task 3 Step 0 warns not to run dev-sync between Task 3 and Task 4 Step 3.

Verified by running: harness loads the real Sync-Repo via AST, patched
version reports the refusal and still commits normal changes, unpatched
control fails all four T1 checks; sync CASE 3/4 plus prior regressions on
/bin/bash 3.2; all embedded scripts parse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
git, base
HOME=/tmp/t11/guard, fix: R11-01..R11-02, first-run gate on both sync scripts

Claude review round 11 (0 high):
- R11-01 Windows dev-sync would run the rewritten twin right after its next
  pull and overwrite all 43 published entries with no snapshot or reconcile.
  Both scripts now refuse any real run until the per-machine marker
  ~/.agents/.sync-v2-ready exists; dry runs are always allowed. On the Mac
  the marker is created only at the end of Task 4 Step 2, so Task 3's
  'do not run dev-sync' warning is now enforced by code. Windows views
  pause visibly until a dedicated prep session.
- R11-02 the twin's index probe no longer writes native stderr, which
  Windows PowerShell 5.1 treats as fatal under ErrorActionPreference=Stop.

Verified by running on /bin/bash 3.2: CASE 5 gate (dry 0, real 2, pool-only
edit survives, no manifest), CASE 1-4, guard, refused-run index unchanged,
deletion workflow; pwsh parse of the twin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
git, fix: R12-01, refuse any DRY_RUN value other than 0 or 1

Claude review round 12 APPROVED with one low finding, fixed because it is a
data-loss route: the bash sync tested DRY against "0" in five places and
"1" in two, so DRY_RUN=true skipped the first-run gate yet still ran the
publish loop's rm -rf. DRY is now validated once, before the gate.

Verified: true/yes/2 refuse with exit 2 and leave the drifted pool copy
intact; 1 stays a dry run; 0 still publishes on a prepared machine.
Control run of the pre-fix script (5779c56) with DRY_RUN=true exited 0,
printed no gate message and replaced the pool copy with a link.

